      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Model.** [Immigrant Share Wage Elasticity](note:immigrant-share-wage-elasticity): $\\log w = \\theta p + \\dots$ with $p = m/(1+m)$, so $\\partial \\log w/\\partial m = \\theta/(1+m)^2$.\n- **Tests.** Computed in Python: $-0.572/1.168^2 = -0.4193$; $m = 1$ gives $-0.143$; $m = 0.5$ gives $-0.2542$."
